1
00:05:10,344 --> 00:05:16,344
Everything you know is about to change forever.

2
00:10:20,689 --> 00:10:26,689
The Chronicles of Narnia: Prince Caspian is a adventure,
family, fantasy film directed by Andrew Adamson.

3
00:15:31,034 --> 00:15:37,034
One year after their incredible adventures in the Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe, Peter, Edmund, Lucy and Susan
Pevensie return to Narnia to aid a young prince whose life has been threatened by the evil King Miraz.

4
00:20:41,379 --> 00:20:47,379
Now, with the help of a colorful cast of new characters, including Trufflehunter the badger and Nikabrik the dwarf, the
Pevensie clan embarks on an incredible quest to ensure that Narnia is returned to its rightful heir.

5
00:25:51,724 --> 00:25:57,724
Peter Pevensie, played by William Moseley.

6
00:31:02,068 --> 00:31:08,068
Susan Pevensie, played by Anna Popplewell.

7
00:36:12,413 --> 00:36:18,413
Edmund Pevensie, played by Skandar Keynes.

8
00:41:22,758 --> 00:41:28,758
Lucy Pevensie, played by Georgie Henley.

9
00:46:33,103 --> 00:46:39,103
Prince Caspian, played by Ben Barnes.

10
00:51:43,448 --> 00:51:49,448
White Witch, played by Tilda Swinton.

11
00:56:53,793 --> 00:56:59,793
The Chronicles of Narnia: Prince Caspian is a 2008 high fantasy film produced by
Walt Disney Pictures and Walden Media, and directed by Andrew Adamson.

12
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:10,137
The screenplay, co-written by Adamson, Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely, is based on the 1951 novel Prince Caspian, the
second published and fourth chronological story in the children's book series The Chronicles of Narnia by C.

13
01:07:14,482 --> 01:07:20,482
The sequel to The Chronicles of Narnia: The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe (2005),
it is the second installment in The Chronicles of Narnia film series.

14
01:12:24,827 --> 01:12:30,827
William Moseley, Anna Popplewell, Skandar Keynes, Georgie Henley, Liam Neeson, and Tilda Swinton reprise their roles from the previous film,
while new cast includes Ben Barnes, Sergio Castellitto, Peter Dinklage, Eddie Izzard, Warwick Davis, Ken Stott, and Vincent Grass.

15
01:17:35,172 --> 01:17:41,172
In the film, the four Pevensie siblings return to Narnia to aid Prince Caspian in
his struggle for the throne against his corrupt uncle, King Miraz.

16
01:22:45,517 --> 01:22:51,517
Work on the script for the film began before The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe was
released, so that filming could begin before the actors grew too old for their parts.

17
01:27:55,862 --> 01:28:01,862
Director Andrew Adamson wanted to make the film more spectacular than the
first, and created an action sequence not in the novel.

18
01:33:06,206 --> 01:33:12,206
The Narnians were designed to look wilder as they have been hiding from
persecution, stressing the darker tone of the sequel.

19
01:38:16,551 --> 01:38:22,551
The filmmakers also took a Spanish influence for the
antagonistic race of the Telmarines.

20
01:43:26,896 --> 01:43:32,896
Filming began in February 2007 in New Zealand, but unlike the previous film, the majority of shooting
took place in Central Europe, because of the larger sets available in those countries.

21
01:48:37,241 --> 01:48:43,241
To keep costs down, Adamson chose to base post-production in the
United Kingdom, because of recent tax credits there.

22
01:53:47,586 --> 01:53:53,586
The Chronicles of Narnia: Prince Caspian premiered on May 7, 2008, at the Ziegfeld Theatre in New York City, before it was
theatrically released on May 16 in the United States and on June 26 in the United Kingdom, by Walt Disney Pictures.

23
01:58:57,931 --> 01:59:03,931
The film received generally positive reviews from critics.

24
02:04:08,275 --> 02:04:14,275
Many praised the performances and visual effects; however, the film's
darker tone and mature themes drew polarizing opinions.

25
02:09:18,620 --> 02:09:24,620
It was a moderate success at the box office, grossing
$55 million during its opening weekend.

26
02:14:28,965 --> 02:14:34,965
By the end of its theatrical run, it had grossed $419.6 million
worldwide, becoming the tenth-highest-grossing film of 2008.

27
02:19:39,310 --> 02:19:45,310
Prince Caspian was the last The Chronicles of Narnia film to be co-produced by Walt Disney Pictures as 20th Century Fox became the distributor for the next film, The Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader
(2010), due to budgetary disputes between Disney and Walden Media, but as a result of Disney eventually purchasing 21st Century Fox in 2019, Disney now owns the rights to all the films in the series.

28
02:24:49,655 --> 02:24:55,655
The film explores themes of witch, sibling
relationship, based on novel or book, faith, lion.
